"Conan!" you whisper, "the rifle...shoot!"
Trembling with fear Conan takes father's double-barrelled rifle, points it at the beast... And at that moment it comes into your head, that it might not be so easy to kill the predator. Maybe it's better to scare him off?
"Wait, don't shoot at him, shoot in the air!"
In another situation, Conan would probably argue, but now he is too scared. A shot rings out. The beast snorts abruptly and steps back.
"Shoot again, another barrel! Shoo, dog, buzz off, A-A-A-A!"
Conan shoots once again. You can hear screams of animals, running away deeper in the forest. You shout as loud as possible, advancing towards the predator. And when you think that you are done for, the beast wavers. Frightful burning eyes are vanished in the thicket, and ringing silence fell upon the glade.